  "scope": "The procedural flook interface embeds the repository-bundled Lua 5.3.5 and Aotus bridge. The FPM wrapper selects the upstream procedural library and bundled C sources, excludes standalone Lua interpreters and the alternative Fortran 2003 interface, and links the system math/dynamic-loading libraries. The checked consumer passes parameters to Lua, executes a short script, retrieves its real and integer results and independently checks 14 and 21. The bundled versions have their own build context; they do not replace the separately catalogued Aotus package. MPL-2.0 and the bundled Aotus/Lua notices are retained. S covers language interoperability.",
  "initial_consumer_findings": [
    "The first consumer attempted to create a global table immediately after lua_init and received SIGSEGV. The checked example follows the author examples by loading a Lua chunk first, creating the parameters table, then accessing it through lua_table. All round-trip values are checked independently. No upstream library code was patched."
  ]
